// ============================================================================
// NEW INTELLIGENCE RUNTIME MODELS — TO BE FROZEN WITH IDENTITY
// ============================================================================
//
// We have established the need for two global runtime concerns:
//
// 1. Processor Execution
//    Immutable execution telemetry: processor/version, entity, executor/model,
//    resolved artifacts, timing, tokens/cost where applicable, retries, status,
//    errors and timestamps.
//
// 2. Intelligence State / History
//    Object-level provenance and lifecycle metadata that should not duplicate the
//    canonical application value: evidence lineage, execution lineage, confidence
//    where applicable, confirmation/manual override, protection/lock state and
//    historical values.
//
// Concrete Prisma models/relations are intentionally deferred until Identity
// objects are mapped to the verified current backend schema. This prevents the
// architecture document from inventing foreign keys or duplicating existing
// application models.
